{"type":"standard","title":"Northern Zaza","displaytitle":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Northern Zaza</span></span>","namespace":{"id":0,"text":""},"wikibase_item":"Q3944007","titles":{"canonical":"Northern_Zaza","normalized":"Northern Zaza","display":"<span lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><span class=\"mw-page-title-main\">Northern Zaza</span></span>"},"pageid":75159296,"thumbnail":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f8/Zaza_DialectsMap-5.gif/330px-Zaza_DialectsMap-5.gif","width":330,"height":149},"originalimage":{"source":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f8/Zaza_DialectsMap-5.gif","width":579,"height":262},"lang":"en","dir":"ltr","revision":"1353987272","tid":"26c3333a-4ee5-11f1-9792-d29a05b7fe87","timestamp":"2026-05-13T16:02:33Z","content_urls":{"desktop":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northern_Zaza","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northern_Zaza?action=history","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northern_Zaza?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Northern_Zaza"},"mobile":{"page":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northern_Zaza","revisions":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:History/Northern_Zaza","edit":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Northern_Zaza?action=edit","talk":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talk:Northern_Zaza"}},"extract":"Northern Zaza, is one of the three primary dialects of the Zaza language, spoken by the Zaza people. The dialect is also referred to as Zonê Ma, Kırmancki, So-Bê, Dımılki, Zazaki, Dersimki, Dersimce or Alevice by its speakers.","extract_html":"<p><b>Northern Zaza</b>, is one of the three primary dialects of the Zaza language, spoken by the Zaza people. The dialect is also referred to as <i>Zonê Ma</i>, <i>Kırmancki, So-Bê, Dımılki, Zazaki, Dersimki, Dersimce</i> or <i>Alevice</i> by its speakers.</p>"}